implementationPlan.description:
Verification, once (DoD 1-3). From the task worktree, run the checkRefs command exactly as written. Its fresh output (the three 'OK: docs/roles/...' lint lines and 'exit: 0') is moe.complete_task's verification evidence.

The command checks, in order:
- the row's diff is exactly docs/DEVELOPMENT.md (`git diff --name-only HEAD`);
- then, in a git-archive snapshot of HEAD with the edited file overlaid (the fix commit's content), nothing in the file still says `minus .bin`;
- the Plugin Bundling block has exactly 2 `├── daemon|proxy/` lines that say 'production packages ... no devDependencies';
- the block names moe-serena-ignore.mjs;
- no line says the daemon never runs git (the daemonGitDocs.test.ts guard);
- `npm run lint` at the snapshot root exits 0.

The command was validated in a scratch clone at 95d91dc2. It exits 1 with no edit, and exits 0 with the edit above (lint: architect 39, worker 30, qa 36 lines).

On failure, fix the doc; never edit the gate. Never run npm install or a build in the shared checkout (project rail).

Self-review, the final step and brief for a 3-line doc fix. Re-read the edited layout block against scripts/bundle-manifest.json (the scripts `files` list, the local-runner and mods excludes, docs/roles, docs/skills) and against both bundlers' daemon/proxy copies.

Check:
- every bundled script file has a line or glob in the block;
- the block names no script the manifest lacks;
- the daemon/proxy wording matches both productionPackages rules: non-dev entries, nested node_modules excluded;
- the `├──`/`│` tree characters and alignment survived the edit (open the rendered block).

If anything changed during this review, re-run step 2's command before moe.complete_task. Put one line in the completion summary naming the three changed lines.
